<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 115 mln stg late help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 115 mln stg late help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with around 115 million stg of unspecified late assistance.</p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.2 BLN    1.25 BLN   1.4 BLN    1.4 BLN</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    150 MLN    700 MLN    1.342 BLN  1.457 BLN</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1     T BILLS   =	    =		60 MLN*  =</p>
<p> BAND 1 BANK BILLS    =	    =		65 MLN*  =</p>
<p> BAND 2 BANK BILLS    =	    =	     367 MLN*  =</p>
<p> BILLS/FRG TO JAN 6   150 MLN#   550 MLN#    150 MLN#  =</p>
<p> UNSPECIFIED ASSISTANCE					  115 MLN</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-15/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
<p># INTEREST RATE - 5-31/32 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
